# QUESTION: Do a real ze hub and managed ze device anchor their SHA-1
# configuration hash chain on initial sync, apply a live V1->V2 hub import via
# diff mode with FoldDiff convergence, heal a reply chain-hash mismatch without
# reconnecting, fall back to full replay when diff is unusable or base is
# missing, and report chain-hash, chain-state, and last-resync in show fleet status?
# WHY NOT A UNIT TEST: Disk ZeFS versioned base lookup, hub write-observer
# config-changed pushes, TLS MuxConn diff/reanchor/full RPC exchanges, device
# transactional reload commits, persisted chain keys on both sides, and SSH CLI
# show fleet status run end to end through the real ze daemons.
# VALIDATES: spec-fleet-10 AC-3, AC-4, AC-5, AC-6, AC-7, AC-8, AC-12.
option=storage:value=disk
option=timeout:value=180s
cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=le test fixture managed/fleet-drift-hash-chain $PORT $PORT2 $PORT3:timeout=180s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=OK: fleet drift hash chain anchored, applied diff update, healed reply mismatch, and fell back to full replay
